CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:Elmo and the Sesame Street friends embark on a once-in-a-lifet
 ime African safari adventure. After adopting an orphaned elephant online\,
  Elmo\, Abby and Nina travel to The Sheldrick Wildlife Trust in Kenya to m
 eet the young elephant and the keepers who care for her. In Sesame Street'
 s first-ever safari\, our friends embark on an unforgettable journey of di
 scovery\, taking them from the caring confines of the elephant sanctuary t
 o the unpredictable African bush\, where they come face to face with some 
 of nature's most iconic wildlife\, including lions\, zebras\, giraffes and
  hippos. For ages 3-8 and their caregivers.\n\nFollowing the screening\, a
  fun crafting activity will take place outside the auditorium.\n\nPresente
 d in collaboration with Sesame Workshop.\n\nFree\n\nPresented by San Franc
 isco Public Library\n\nFree\nSan Francisco Public Library\n\nDetails: http
 s://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/10/film-sesame-street-and-the-great-elepha
 nt-adventure-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay\n\nAlso listed on:\n- https://sf.fu
 ncheap.com/free-kids-safari-film-sesame-streets-elephant-adventure-crafts-
 sf-main-library/
