DESCRIPTION:Pene Pati & filmmaker Rebecca Tansley IN PERSON Sun\, Oct 11!\
 n\nTenor: My Name is Pati\, a new documentary that tells the remarkable st
 ory of Samoan tenor brothers and former SF Opera Adler Fellows\, Pene Pati
  & Amitai Pati\, from humble origins in the South Pacific to the world’s
  greatest opera stages. Weaving intimate family archive footage with behin
 d-the-scenes observations and soaring performances\, the film blends humor
  and heart to reveal how the power of family and cultural pride\, determin
 ation\, and resilience can yield rewards when chasing an unlikely dream. T
 enor Pene Pati\, performing as the Chevalier des Grieux in Jules Massenet
 ’s Manon at the San Francisco Opera (10/15-11/1)\, will be here in perso
 n with Tenor filmmaker Rebecca Tansley on opening night.\n\nTICKETS ON SAL
 E\, NOW.\n\nRuntime\n\n1h 43m\n\nYear\n\n2026\n\nDirector\n\nRebecca Tansl
 ey\n\nFormat\n\nDCP\n\nCountry\n\nNew Zealand\n\nFirst Showing\n\nOctober 
 11\, 2026\n\nCategories\n\nFeatured\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/event
 s/2026/10/11/tenor-my-name-is-pati-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay\n\nAlso liste
 d on:\n- https://sf.funcheap.com/david-cay-johnston-ian-masters-oakland/
