SUMMARY:Repo! The Genetic Opera
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261011T213000
DTSTAMP:20261012T110211Z
UID:dothebay-17830861@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:In the year 2056 – the not-so-distant future – an epidemic
  of organ failures devastates the planet. Out of the tragedy\, a savior em
 erges: GeneCo\, a biotech company that offers organ transplants\, for a pr
 ice. Those who miss their payments are scheduled for repossession and hunt
 ed by villainous Repo Men. In a world where surgery addicts are hooked on 
 painkilling drugs and murder is sanctioned by law\, a sheltered young girl
  searches for the cure to her own rare disease as well as information abou
 t her family's mysterious history. After being sucked into the haunting wo
 rld of GeneCo\, she is unable to turn back\, as all of her questions will 
 be answered at the wildly anticipated spectacular event: The Genetic Opera
 . The film features a goth rock/opera score sung by genre favorites Paul S
 orvino\, Anthony Stewart Head\, Sarah Brightman\, and Bill Moseley.\n\nDet
 ails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/11/repo-the-genetic-opera-ticket
 s\nSource: DoTheBay
