DESCRIPTION:Celebrating the 50th anniversary of The Band’s legendary far
 ewell concert\, Martin Scorsese’s The Last Waltz captures an unforgettab
 le night at Bill Graham’s Winterland Ballroom in San Francisco\, creatin
 g one of cinema’s most influential music documentaries.\n\nGuests Expect
 edThe evening begins with a special conversation moderated by legendary mu
 sic journalist Ben Fong-Torres featuring cinematographer Hiro Narita\, an 
 onstage camera operator for The Last Waltz\, music critic and journalist J
 oel Selvin\, and the film’s Executive Producer and former tour manager f
 or The Band Jonathan Taplin. These luminaries will gather for the first ti
 me to share anecdotes about their in-person experiences at the Winterland 
 Ballroom in 1976\, providing a unique perspective of a historic event befo
 re we screen a 4K restoration of Martin Scorsese’s The Last Waltz.\n\n$2
 6.73\nSFFILM Presents:\n\nTickets: https://sffilm.org/event/the-last-waltz
 /\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/21/scorsese-s-legendary-mu
 sic-doc-the-last-waltz-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
