BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:30th Arab Film Festival at SF’s AMC Kabuki (Nov. 5-14)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T211500
DTSTAMP:20261014T050109Z
UID:funcheap-1642380@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Movies
DESCRIPTION:El Sett (courtesy of Watermelon Pictures)The 30th anniversary 
 edition of the Arab Film Festival (AFF30)\, runs November 5–14\, 2026 wi
 th more than 30 events across San Francisco\, Oakland\, and the South Bay\
 , including film screenings\, filmmaker conversations\, panels\, special p
 resentations and community events\, with select programming available virt
 ually.\n\nGeneral admission to most screenings: $20\nOpening Night (11/5 a
 t AMC Kabuki): $45\nAll-Access Pass: $180\nVIP All-Access Pass: $250\nVirt
 ual-Only Pass: $60\n\nAFF30 will open Thursday\, November 5 at AMC Kabuki 
 in San Francisco with Marwan Hamed’s El Sett\, a sweeping cinematic port
 rait of legendary Egyptian singer Umm Kulthum\, starring Mona Zaki. Celebr
 ated Egyptian producer Mohamed Hefzy will be honored on Opening Night with
  the inaugural AFMI Luminary Award for Cultural Impact and will attend as 
 a special guest.\nAFF30 will also feature a special presentation of Edward
  Said: Between Worlds\, directed by Maiken Baird\, on Sunday\, November 8 
 at the Castro Theatre in San Francisco\, followed by a panel with Baird\, 
 producer Sarah Mowaswes and Edward Said’s family.\n\nAcclaimed Saudi fil
 mmaker Haifaa Al Mansour will serve as Jury Chair for the 30th Arab Film F
 estival\, leading a jury that includes filmmakers Mounia Akl\, Shihan Fé 
 Blanca Fahim\, Basil Khalil\, Jehane Noujaim and Bao Nguyen\; visual artis
 t Nabila Abuljadayel\; producers Rémi Grellety and Conrad Montgomery\; wr
 iter and playwright Sabrina Mahfouz\; and actor and producer David Oyelowo
 ....\n\n$45.00\n\nTickets: https://arabfilmfestival.org\nDetails: https://
 sf.funcheap.com/30th-arab-film-festival-sfs-amc-kabuki-nov-514/\nSource: F
 uncheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/El-Set
 t-Opening-Night-AFF30.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261014T050109Z
LOCATION:AMC Kabuki Cinemas\, 1881 Post St\, San Francisco\, CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/30th-arab-film-festival-sfs-amc-kabuki-nov-514
 /
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Elsinore
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T203000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17858094@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:Another Planet Entertainment and Frameline present\nElsinore\n
 \nThursday\, November 5 | The Castro\n\nFounded in 1977\, Frameline is a S
 an Francisco-based nonprofit media arts organization dedicated to the deve
 lopment\, exhibition\, distribution\, and preservation of LGBTQ+ cinema an
 d independent queer media.\n\nFrameline Fall Showcase presents Elsinore\n\
 nBy 1989 acclaimed Scottish actor Ian Charleson (a sensational Andrew Scot
 t\, All of Us Strangers)\, who had career-defining roles in Oscar-winning 
 pictures Chariots of Fire (1981) and Gandhi (1982)\, yearns for his next g
 reat role. For Charleson\, a gay man with AIDS\, navigating Hollywood and 
 keeping his personal life private is a minefield\, and he’s drawn to the
  idea of revisiting his stage-actor roots. When Daniel Day Lewis abandons 
 Richard Eyre’s (Johnny Flynn\, Ripley) production of Hamlet at the Natio
 nal Theatre mid-performance\, Charleson is poised to take over the play’
 s title role.\n\nBut the actor’s ambitious return is halted when he deve
 lops Kaposi’s sarcoma\, prompting his doctor (Oscar winner Olivia Colman
 \, The Favourite) to forbid him from taking on such a strenuous role. Feat
 uring memorable supporting turns from Joe Locke(Heartstopper) and David Da
 wson (My Policeman)\, who plays renowned queer filmmaker Derek Jarman\, Si
 mon Stone’s latest is a deeply resonant film about the power of art and 
 human connection in the face of mortality\, all moored by a career-best\, 
 Oscar-worthy performance from Scott.\n\nAnother Planet Entertainment and F
 rameline present\nListed time is doors\n\nTickets: https://thecastro.com/e
 vents/elsinore-261105\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/5/elsi
 nore-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7619917;-122.4347365
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34497414/95b54625-d36e-479b-b8a8-d5604985cd80.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003107Z
LOCATION:The Castro\, 429 Castro St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94114
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/5/elsinore-tickets
END:VEVENT
