BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hold on to Your Music: A Mother's Legacy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T190000
DTSTAMP:20261015T212936Z
UID:dothebay-17956737@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the San Francisco premiere of Hold On To Your Musi
 c: A Mother's Legacy\, including a live performance by internationally acc
 laimed concert pianist Mona Golabek.\n\nVienna\, 1938. The parents of 14-y
 ear-old piano prodigy Lisa Jura faced an unimaginable choice: which of the
 ir three daughters to send to safety on the Kindertransport. They chose Li
 sa. She arrived alone in London\, carrying her dreams\, memories of her fa
 mily\, and her mother's parting words: "Hold on to your music."\n\nDirecte
 d by Academy Award nominated Josh Aronson and Emmy Award winner Adam Wood\
 , the film tells Lisa's remarkable story through rare archival footage\, n
 ewly restored recordings\, and performances by her daughter\, Mona Golabek
 . Drawing on Golabek's best-selling book and acclaimed stage production\, 
 The Pianist of Willesden Lane\, it celebrates the enduring power of music 
 and a mother's love - a story that has reached more than 20 million people
  worldwide.\n\nFollowing the screening and live performance\, Golabek join
 s director Josh Aronson and producer Susan Solomon Libitzky in conversatio
 n with executive producer\, Dr. Anita Friedman.\n\n$30.\n\nPresented by JC
 C SF\n\n$30.\nJCC SF\n\nTickets: https://www.jccsf.org/event/hold-on-to-yo
 ur-music-a-mothers-legacy/\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/8
 /hold-on-to-your-music-a-mother-s-legacy-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.787374;-122.4473551
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34962749/d3229d73-be80-448c-ae4d-f9ed0e5d0864.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261015T212936Z
LOCATION:Jewish Community Center of San Francisco\, 3200 California Street
 \, San Francisco\, CA\, 94118
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/8/hold-on-to-your-music-a-mother-s
 -legacy-tickets
